Anicel's own, step one of "the screen comes back": the Windows embedder
says that the EGL context its screen is drawn with is lost.

As shipped, a failed EGL call logs a line (LogEGLError) and returns
false: nothing tells the app, and the window stays on its last picture
(board a-real-gpu-reset-went-unheard-on-the-main-pc; the user's release
app, 2026-11-16, 11-18, 11-22). Every failed EGL call of the embedder
passes LogEGLError, so the loss is said there, once a process: each
top-level window of the process is posted the window message registered
by the name "FlutterWindowsEglContextLost", its WPARAM the EGL error.
The app's runner registers the same name and says it to Dart where it
says its own watch's word (windows/runner/flutter_window.cpp).

One file, no header and no ABI changed: what an upgrade of Flutter costs
is this hunk laid again. Base blob 85af46f6858a3 = this tree's file at
3.47.4.

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/egl/egl.cc b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/egl/egl.cc
index 85af46f..f08f3c5 100644
--- a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/egl/egl.cc
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/egl/egl.cc
@@ -4,8 +4,12 @@
 
 #include "flutter/shell/platform/windows/egl/egl.h"
 
+#include <windows.h>
+
 #include <EGL/egl.h>
 
+#include <atomic>
+
 #include "flutter/fml/logging.h"
 
 namespace flutter {
@@ -50,10 +54,42 @@ const char* EGLErrorToString(EGLint error) {
   return "Unknown";
 }
 
+// [anicel 0002] The embedder never hears that the context its screen is
+// drawn with is lost: a call fails, a line is logged, and the window stays
+// on its last picture. Every failed EGL call of this embedder passes
+// LogEGLError, so the loss is said there, once a process: each top-level
+// window of the process is posted the message registered by this name,
+// its WPARAM the EGL error. A runner hears it by registering the same
+// name; one that does not is posted a message it has no handler for.
+constexpr wchar_t kContextLostMessageName[] = L"FlutterWindowsEglContextLost";
+
+BOOL CALLBACK PostContextLost(HWND window, LPARAM message) {
+  DWORD process = 0;
+  ::GetWindowThreadProcessId(window, &process);
+  if (process == ::GetCurrentProcessId()) {
+    ::PostMessageW(window, static_cast<UINT>(message), EGL_CONTEXT_LOST, 0);
+  }
+  return TRUE;
+}
+
+void TellContextLost() {
+  static std::atomic<bool> told{false};
+  if (told.exchange(true)) {
+    return;
+  }
+  const UINT message = ::RegisterWindowMessageW(kContextLostMessageName);
+  if (message != 0) {
+    ::EnumWindows(PostContextLost, static_cast<LPARAM>(message));
+  }
+}
+
 }  // namespace
 
 void LogEGLError(std::string_view message) {
   const EGLint error = ::eglGetError();
+  if (error == EGL_CONTEXT_LOST) {
+    TellContextLost();
+  }
   return FML_LOG(ERROR) << "EGL Error: " << EGLErrorToString(error) << " ("
                         << error << ") " << message;
 }
